# common-ui Reuse

Shared frontend code lives in `frontend/projects/common-ui/`. **Search here before creating parallel utilities.**

## Base classes

| Class | Extend for |
|-------|------------|
| `BaseComponent` | All components — auth signal, `extractErrorMessage()`, date formats, mobile breakpoint |
| `BaseApiService` | HTTP API clients — `HttpClient`, `EnvironmentService`, `queryToParams()` |
| `BaseListComponent<T>` | Admin list pages — paging, filters, selection, responsive columns |
| `BaseEditComponent<T>` | Admin create/edit/detail — route param load, form lifecycle |

Admin components extend bases; HTTP services go in `common-ui/services/`, not inside `admin-ui`.

## Before building new…

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Modal/dialog | `DialogService` + `DialogRef` in `common-ui/dialog/` |
| Enum label in template | `StatusEnumPipe` or contract enum + pipe |
| Relative time | `TimeAgoPipe` |
| JSON display | `PrettyJsonPipe` |
| String/date/number helpers | `common-ui/utils/` |
| DTOs, enums, queries | `@app/contracts` |

## Errors in UI

Use `this.extractErrorMessage(error)` from `BaseComponent` in snackbars — matches backend `{ code, message }` shape.

## Import style

Relative imports across projects, e.g. `../../../common-ui/services/users.service` — `common-ui` is not a separate npm package.

## Rules

- Reusable logic → `common-ui`; admin-only UI → `admin-ui/features/`.
- Do not duplicate contract types or enum maps in app code.
